part prices
  tally 2
  note "Fund prices, one reading input over the unit kind funds (L §3.2): the market files' rows that a question reads, each citing its file and line (the files are not imported whole; the Wektor files' decimal comma and day-first dates are a dialect, O:A-1)."
  note "Forecast (A-12): each fund's price moves on each month's last day by the path's rate and is then rounded to the places its fund quotes in (story § The forecast, item 3). The forecast's rules test fc_on, which only the scenario forecast sets (scenarios/forecast.tally): a rule pointing at the scenario's version with v, as L §6.4 allows, is refused by the reference interpreter (fault F3)."
  note "px_round: the story doesn't say how a moved price is rounded to its places (an unstated mode is an axis)."

axis px_round
  half-up "a moved price is rounded to its fund's places, half up"
  down "a moved price is cut to its fund's places"

input fc_base: month question "From which month's last price does the forecast move prices?"

input mk[u in funds]: num DUK/u reading question "What is this fund's price on this valuation day (tmp/cases/market/<fund>.csv)?"

input path_rate[m in month]: num question "By what rate does every fund's price move on this month's last day (story § The forecast, item 3)?"

input px_step[u in funds]: num DUK/u question "To what step does this fund quote its price?"

def pm[u in funds, m in month]: num DUK/u at end_of(m) - 1 day
  note "the fund's price at the end of month m: the market's reading that day; in the forecast, the month before's moved by the path's rate, rounded to the fund's step"
  rule market_end = mk[u]
  rule moved beats market_end = round(pm[u, m - 1] * (1 + path_rate[m]), px_step[u], px_round) when fc_on and pos(m) > 1 and m > fc_base

def px[u in funds, d in day]: num DUK/u at d
  note "the fund's price on day d: the market's reading; in the forecast, the last month-end price on or before d (the workplace plans' fund stays outside the forecast, story § The forecast, item 4)"
  rule market = mk[u]
  rule forecast beats market = if d == end_of(month_of(d)) - 1 day then pm[u, month_of(d)] else pm[u, month_of(d) - 1] when fc_on and month_of(d) > fc_base and u != wcp

version fund_steps
  cite market_files
  governs always
  known 2021-01-01
  px_step[bnd] = 0.01 "brz-bnd-a.csv: prices to 2 places"
  px_step[div] = 0.01 "brz-div-d.csv: prices to 2 places"
  px_step[em] = 0.0001 "wek-em-a.csv: prices to 4 places"
  px_step[glb] = 0.01 "brz-glb-a.csv: prices to 2 places"
  px_step[idx] = 0.0001 "wek-idx-d.csv: prices to 4 places"
  px_step[mm] = 0.01 "brz-mm-a.csv: prices to 2 places"
  px_step[wcp] = 0.0001 "wek-wcp-2055.csv: prices to 4 places"

version mk_20230912
